name 'iterating-with-ai-postassessment-q2_2025'

question 'When reviewing AI-generated pseudocode for a loop, you notice there is no "update" step for the loop variable. What is the most likely result if this code is run?'

right 'The loop will become "infinite" because the stopping condition will never be reached.'
wrong 'The loop will finish faster than expected.'
wrong 'The loop will run once and then stop correctly.'
wrong 'The loop will skip every other item in the dataset.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 1

If the state of the loop (the variable being checked) never changes toward the stopping condition, the condition remains true forever, resulting in an infinite loop.
MARKDOWN
